  --channel ID     one channel id (default: every member channel)
  --full           re-fetch from the beginning, not only what is newer
  --limit N, -n    how far back a first sync or --full reaches (default 1000)

  Output: {"connection", "channels", "new", "detail": [{"channel",
  "fetched", "new"}]}.
""" + _HELP_SELECT + _HELP_EXIT_READ + _HELP_STORE + """
  Examples:
    slacker sync
    slacker sync --channel <channel> --full --limit 5000
""",
    "send": """\
slacker send <channel> <text> [--thread TS] [--broadcast] [--connection <id>]

  Send a message to a DM, group DM or channel; with --thread, reply in that
  thread, and with --broadcast also post the reply to the channel. Text `-`
  reads it from stdin; empty text exits 6. Answers the new ts.

  --thread TS   the parent ts: reply in its thread
  --broadcast   with --thread, also post the reply to the channel (exit 6
                without --thread)

  Output: {"ok": true, "connection", "channel", "ts", "thread_ts",
  "broadcast", "stored"}; stored is whether the store gained the row.
""" + _HELP_WRITE + _HELP_SELECT + _HELP_STORE + """
  Examples:
    slacker send <channel> "On it."
    printf 'Done.' | slacker send <channel> - --thread <ts> --broadcast
